[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496208812","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99646#issuecomment-2496208812","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99646","id":2496208812,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UyR-s","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-24T20:12:51Z","updated_at":"2024-11-24T20:12:51Z","body":"Do you have a method for testing this like a test project?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496208812/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496237522","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99646#issuecomment-2496237522","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99646","id":2496237522,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UyY_S","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-24T21:08:47Z","updated_at":"2024-11-24T21:42:51Z","body":"> Do you have a method for testing this like a test project?\r\n\r\nFor stability test just spawn, change, and delete (ten) thousands of `NavigationRegion3D`, `NavigationLink3D`, `NavigationAgent3D` and `NavigationObstacle3D` nodes at random intervals between physics steps until your CPU catches fire.\r\n\r\nAlso helps when the reported debug monitor navigation section numbers make sense after every change.\r\n\r\nThe `--test -test-suite= *[Navigation]*` already confirmed that there are no (major?) sync errors because those tests expect a valid result directly after a single sync, else the tests start screaming which I had multiple times while working on this.\r\n\r\nPerformance testing in a vacuum is mostly pointless for this PR as it was sliced from a bigger PR for async synchronisation  missing the main accompanying pieces. I am piecemealing that larger PR atm with smaller PRs like here to escape the rebase hellscape as best as I can.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496237522/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2501496004","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99646#issuecomment-2501496004","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99646","id":2501496004,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VGczE","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-26T17:13:34Z","updated_at":"2024-11-26T17:13:34Z","body":"Even if it's redundant in isolation, some performance metrics would be nice — if only to ensure that this isn't *regressing* current behavior. I have no real reason to believe there's been a regression, but I believe this is a practice we're wanting to employ for performance PRs moving forward","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2501496004/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2501595480","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99646#issuecomment-2501595480","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99646","id":2501595480,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VG1FY","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-26T17:55:58Z","updated_at":"2024-11-26T17:55:58Z","body":"In general I agree but as mentioned a performance test for this PR is mostly pointless in isolation without all the other async update related PRs that follow. If this is more about the performance label we can just remove it from this PR.\r\n\r\nIt is like the theoretical discussion if adding code that starts and joins a thread costs more and causes a performance  \"regression\". Sure it does, but that is not the point, the point is to offload things from the main thread because the single-threaded way is already no longer working. You can't do async updates while the map sync is just for-looping over everything like a donkey kong.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/